<title>USA: St Joseph hogs up $1.50 - USDA.</title>
<headline>St Joseph hogs up $1.50 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>ST JOSEPH 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said compared with Wednesday, barrows and gilts were $1.50 higher. Top $53.50 per cwt.</p>
<p>Spring record low temperatures with freezing snow and rain curtailed marketings. Another blizzard up North. Interior Iowa only moved 100,000 Wednesday.</p>
<p>    US 1-3	230-270 lbs    53.00-53.50</p>
<p>    US 2-3	270-290 lbs    51.50-52.50</p>
<p>Sows - scarce.</p>
<p>Boars - scarce.</p>
</text>
